###  Commits on Jun 29, 2026 

  * ####  [ Fix TypeObject owned sequence cleanup ](/eclipse-cyclonedds/cyclonedds/commit/1ec5d3521d7df768ac2afff66151a6d10b60cf24 "Fix TypeObject owned sequence cleanup

TypeObject generation allocates sequence buffers that are later released
by the generic CDR sample finalizer. If validation or fuzz mutations
shorten _length before finalization, the finalizer still needs _maximum
to describe the allocated elements so it can walk nested owned fields
before freeing the buffer.

Set _maximum consistently for generated owned TypeObject sequences and
copied annotation sequences. Add a regression that shortens annotated
enum and bitmask sequences before finalizing the TypeObject, matching
the OSS-Fuzz leak shape.")

